NUM-08: book only the excess over full volume as overflow when a node first floods

DWSolver::commitNodeDepthState() set a non-ponding node's overflow to the
whole net inflow of the step (dV/dt) and its volume to the full volume. On
the step the node first floods it started below full, so the volume that
filled it was counted as storage and again as overflow. Set the overflow to
(old_volume + dV - rpt_full_volume)/dt, not below zero, as the 5.3.0 patch
does. Steps that start full, and plain junctions (full volume 0), are
unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-08_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydraulics/DynamicWave.cpp b/src/engine/hydraulics/DynamicWave.cpp
index c83bf96..0364a44 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydraulics/DynamicWave.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydraulics/DynamicWave.cpp
@@ -4224,7 +4224,9 @@ void DWSolver::commitNodeDepthState(SimulationContext& ctx, int node_idx,
     if (y_new > y_max) {
         if (!can_pond) {
             // Non-ponded flooding: cap at max, excess is overflow
-            nodes.overflow[ui] = dV / dt;
+            // (what is left after the node fills to its full volume)
+            nodes.overflow[ui] = std::max(0.0, nodes.old_volume[ui] + dV -
+                                          t.rpt_full_volume) / dt;
             nodes.volume[ui] = t.rpt_full_volume;
             y_new = y_max;
         } else {
